{"type":"standard","title":"Embu language","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Embu language</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q35318","titles":{"canonical":"Embu_language","normalized":"Embu language","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Embu language</span></span>"},"pageid":28266844,"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1349967703","tid":"7716e0cb-3c1a-11f1-8a3f-29c1d3659186","timestamp":"2026-04-19T18:06:19Z","description":"Bantu language spoken in Kenya","description_source":"local","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Embu_language","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Embu_language?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Embu_language?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Embu_language"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Embu_language","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Embu_language","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Embu_language?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Embu_language"}},"extract":"Embu, also known as Kîembu, is a Bantu language of Kenya. It is spoken by the Embu people, also known as the Aembu. Speakers of the Embu language can also be found in neighboring districts/counties and in the diaspora.","extract_html":"<p><b>Embu</b>, also known as <b>Kîembu</b>, is a Bantu language of Kenya. It is spoken by the Embu people, also known as the Aembu. Speakers of the Embu language can also be found in neighboring districts/counties and in the diaspora.</p>"}